    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n5 Bed Detached house of c. 198 m² in the popular village of Newtownforbes just off the N4 Dublin Road convenient to Longford Town, local shops and amenities.\n\nThe house features a large sitting room with an open fireplace that opens via double doors into the dining room. This room also has double glass doors opening out to the east facing rear garden, there are also double doors into the Kitchen, this allows for an open plan enhanced with new floors throughout these three rooms. \n\nThe kitchen features a huge window looking out to the rear garden that floods the room with light. There are maple wood built in units with an island unit and integrated appliances. This is complemented by a utility room plumbed for washer & dryer. \n\nThere is also ground floor reception room that could be used as a study / games room or a sixth bedroom if required.\n\nUpstairs there are two ensuite bedrooms and the main bedroom also has a walk in wardrobe. The other three bedrooms are served by a fully tiled family bathroom. One of the bedrooms is single sized and could be an ideal home office to take advantage of high speed fibre broadband available here.\n\nThe house has been recently refurbished, freshly painted, new flooring on the ground floor and refinished wood floors on the first floor level.\n\n\nServices:\n• Mains Water and Sewerage, \n• Oil fired central heating \n• Fibre to the home high speed broadband available\n\n\nOutside: \nSituated at the end of a small cu de sac, there is a park green to the rear and mature trees along the side of the house. \nTo the front of the house there is a driveway with parking space for a number of cars. \n\n\nLocation:\nThe house is located just off the N4 Dublin Sligo Road, easy walking distance to the local shops & pubs. Newtownforbes takes its name from the Forbes family, also known as the Earl of Granard, and have been resident in Castleforbes since 1691. \n\nNewtownforbes is a popular residential location with an excellent Primary school, and modern GAA complex, which the house is very close to. The village has local shops, post office, restaurant and churches. Being on the N4 Dublin Sligo Road there are bus stops along the main street and Longford town centre is just a 5 minute drive. The village has an active tidy town group and recently helped develop a heritage & biodiversity trail walk that is convenient to the house.\n\n\nEircode: N39 X459 \nGPS: 53.7630, -7.8409\n\n\nBER C2\nBER No. 112517313\nEnergy Performance Indicator: 175.31 kWh/m²/yr."
      },
